{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p1-61af30f3","text":"Task: model MCP23017 interrupts:
- GPINTEN (0x04/0x05): interrupt-on-change enable per pin.
- INTCON (0x08/0x09): 0 = compare against previous pin value (any change), 1 = compare against DEFVAL.
- DEFVAL (0x06/0x07): default comparison value when INTCON=1.
- INTF (0x0E/0x0F): interrupt flag, set when a pin matches the condition; cleared by reading INTF (or INTCAP).
- INTCAP (0x10/0x11): captures the port value when the interrupt occurred; reading clears INTF.
- IOCON (0x0A/0x0B): MIRROR, ODR, INTPOL etc. affect INTA/INTB behavior.
- GPINTEN default 0 → no interrupts.

Also the pins INTA/INTB: the current definition has only VCC/GND/SDA/SCL + 16 ports. The module as sold (e.g., the common blue breakout) has INTA/INTB but the definition omits them. To "drive the INTA/INTB pins" I'd need pins on the definition. The user explicitly asks to drive them. The definition's pins are used for the artwork/holes. Adding INTA/INTB pins changes the definition's pin list → the existing module test asserts the exact pin list. Also artwork ModuleBody draws from definition pins, so they'd appear on the bench.

Scope decision: The request says "so an input change sets INTF and drives the INTA/INTB pins". So I need:
1. Register model: GPINTEN, INTCON, DEFVAL, INTF, INTCAP, IOCON (mirror/polarity at least).
